1
00:01:55,916 --> 00:01:57,916


2
00:02:07,739 --> 00:02:09,820
The sea is so vast and nice.

3
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:38,485
Put a baby turtle on the mama's back!

4
00:02:38,509 --> 00:02:41,165
Put a little turtle on the mama's back!

5
00:02:41,189 --> 00:02:44,500
Splash some water on them, splash, splash, splash!

6
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:46,020
That's so mean!

7
00:02:46,215 --> 00:02:47,540
Wait!

8
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,320
Hey!

9
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,740
Come on, keep your head up!

10
00:02:49,741 --> 00:02:51,140
Apologize and I'll forgive you!

11
00:02:51,141 --> 00:02:52,460
Say something!

12
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:53,575
What was that?

13
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,200
You little runt!

14
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:54,973
Back off!

15
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:56,146
I'll punch you!

16
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:57,080
Fine by me!

17
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,700
All right!

18
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:02,820
What is it?

19
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:03,560
What's this?

20
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:08,121
Swish, swish, swish... And down!

21
00:03:08,950 --> 00:03:13,420
Look, it's not much, but I earned this money tending sheep.

22
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,300
I'll give you this, so please let Kogame-san go.

23
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:17,660
Only ten yen?!

24
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,400
Don't underestimate me!

25
00:03:19,401 --> 00:03:20,720
Hold still!

26
00:03:20,745 --> 00:03:21,880
I'll take you down!

27
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:37,046
I don't think it's right to pick on the weak.

28
00:03:37,244 --> 00:03:39,020
I-It spoke!

29
00:03:39,060 --> 00:03:40,793
I don't think fighting is good.

30
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:47,440
I don't think it's right to bully the weak. I don't think it's right to bully the weak.

31
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:51,020
Come on, pull yourself together.

32
00:03:52,255 --> 00:03:54,583
You know, I thought I'd save Kame-san

33
00:03:54,607 --> 00:03:57,120
and his friends, just like Urashima Taro.

34
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,160
But it turned out the exact opposite.

35
00:03:59,350 --> 00:04:02,000
I've been looking for someone like you.

36
00:04:02,025 --> 00:04:03,260
Please save me!

37
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Save you?

38
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:08,300
Come, off to the Dragon Palace!
The Dragon Palace?

39
00:04:09,075 --> 00:04:10,960
Whoa, this is crazy!

40
00:04:11,213 --> 00:04:13,340
I have no idea what's going on!

41
00:04:13,554 --> 00:04:16,260
I told you, I can't swim!

42
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:18,079
Sapphire!

43
00:04:23,293 --> 00:04:25,133
Tink!

44
00:04:25,773 --> 00:04:27,348
Tink!

45
00:04:27,566 --> 00:04:28,859
Tink!

46
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:30,420
Lord Sapphire, where are you going?

47
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,440
I'm going to play with Tink!

48
00:04:32,655 --> 00:04:33,960
None of that matters!

49
00:04:34,419 --> 00:04:36,786
Be that as it may, Lord Sapphire...

50
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:42,096
Tink!

51
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:43,940
Wait up!

52
00:04:46,610 --> 00:04:48,640
I'm not Urashima Taro!

53
00:04:48,770 --> 00:04:50,700
If I go to the Dragon Palace, I'll drown!

54
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:54,619
Please, just bear with it a little longer to help us out.

55
00:04:55,065 --> 00:04:57,573
But the Dragon Palace is at the bottom of the sea, right?

56
00:04:58,210 --> 00:04:59,780
I'm scared of the ocean floor.

57
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:15,233
Sapphire! Help me!

58
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:30,920
Oh! Is that where you were? Wake up! Hey, wake up! Come on, wake up!

59
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:46,960
Are you awake?

60
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,220
Is this... the place?

61
00:05:49,385 --> 00:05:50,713
It's the Dragon Kingdom.

62
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:53,940
So we really are at the bottom of the sea.

63
00:05:54,735 --> 00:05:57,200
But I'm not drowning...

64
00:06:00,090 --> 00:06:01,516
Come on, let's go to the Dragon Palace!

65
00:06:01,541 --> 00:06:04,016
The elders and the Sea God are waiting!

66
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,005
The Sea God?

67
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:06,780
That's right, the God of the Sea!

68
00:06:06,965 --> 00:06:07,965
A god?

69
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:23,740
Sharks! Run!

70
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:34,580
Wait!

71
00:06:35,610 --> 00:06:37,793
I hear it, I hear it!

72
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:41,100
A ship is passing overhead.

73
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:45,740
Hey, sharks! Drag that ship down here!

74
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:50,386
Maybe I can eat some crispy biscuits for a change.

75
00:06:53,053 --> 00:06:54,673
Hey, turtle.

76
00:06:55,485 --> 00:06:56,485
W-What is it?

77
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:59,520
What is that tiny human you've got with you?

78
00:06:59,570 --> 00:07:01,720
T-This is my guest!

79
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:03,084
A guest?

80
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:04,073
Don't make me laugh.

81
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,860
Give it to me! No way!

82
00:07:06,241 --> 00:07:06,861
Shut up!

83
00:07:08,170 --> 00:07:10,820
The more I look at it, the cuter this human is.

84
00:07:11,265 --> 00:07:13,666
I'll put it in my zoo.

85
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:14,660
Hand it over!

86
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
No!

87
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:18,357
Wait!

88
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,106
Hey, Anko.

89
00:07:41,490 --> 00:07:43,806
A little turtle and a rare creature came by, didn't they?

90
00:07:43,925 --> 00:07:45,326
I don't know!

91
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:46,255
Don't play dumb with me!

92
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,280
I'm going to search you.

93
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,860
Human food.

94
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,160
Biscuits.

95
00:08:01,330 --> 00:08:02,979
Soggy, just as I thought.

96
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:08,160
Ah, so noisy! I can't even take a nap.

97
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,080
Help me!

98
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:17,120
Who's thrashing around inside my stomach?

99
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,033
Thank you.

100
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:25,480
You saved me.

101
00:08:26,090 --> 00:08:27,540
And now my stomach hurts...

102
00:08:27,564 --> 00:08:29,160
Come on, let's go to Dragon Palace.

103
00:08:47,389 --> 00:08:48,389
Here it is.

104
00:08:48,695 --> 00:08:50,540
Dragon Gate Castle is really run-down, isn't it?

105
00:08:50,725 --> 00:08:52,220
It used to be grand.

106
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:55,776
It ended up like this because of those Sharks. That's right.

107
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,320
Great Sea God, we have guests!

108
00:09:03,444 --> 00:09:05,080
We brought visitors!

109
00:09:05,350 --> 00:09:07,440
Great Sea God!

110
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:20,520
Haven't I told you that yelling will break the castle?

111
00:09:20,635 --> 00:09:22,865
Ah, welcome! Glad you're safe.

112
00:09:23,049 --> 00:09:27,013
Hey, I thought Princess Otohime was at Dragon Gate Castle.

113
00:09:27,509 --> 00:09:29,920
Princess Otohime is the Great Sea God's daughter.

114
00:09:30,834 --> 00:09:33,500
Oh, so she really is here after all!

115
00:09:33,615 --> 00:09:34,940
I'd love to meet her.

116
00:09:35,489 --> 00:09:37,826
Princess Otohime isn't here.

117
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:38,940
Is she dead?

118
00:09:39,169 --> 00:09:40,499
She's not dead!

119
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:41,792
It's just...

120
00:09:41,816 --> 00:09:42,821
What's wrong?

121
00:09:49,510 --> 00:09:52,160
I am Neptune, the Sea God.

122
00:09:52,270 --> 00:09:53,813
Welcome, honored guest.

123
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,720
You seem like a kind-hearted person.

124
00:09:55,885 --> 00:09:56,665
I'm Tink.

125
00:09:56,689 --> 00:09:57,898
Tink, is it?

126
00:09:57,922 --> 00:10:01,520
You certainly don't seem like an ordinary human.

127
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:03,300
You see...

128
00:10:03,545 --> 00:10:05,120
Truth is, I'm not human.

129
00:10:05,245 --> 00:10:05,940
I'm an angel.

130
00:10:06,205 --> 00:10:07,124
Well, a former angel.

131
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,060
An angel?

132
00:10:08,275 --> 00:10:10,940
Oh, what a blessing!

133
00:10:11,065 --> 00:10:15,520
Sir Tink, please save my daughter, Otohime.

134
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:17,180
Save her?

135
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,546
What on earth happened?

136
00:10:18,958 --> 00:10:21,033
Come this way, Sir Tink.

137
00:10:37,029 --> 00:10:38,860
Right over here, Sir Tink.

138
00:10:46,529 --> 00:10:48,840
Otohime is inside here.

139
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,220
Where?

140
00:10:50,345 --> 00:10:51,600
I don't see anything.

141
00:10:52,209 --> 00:10:53,986
Hey, is Ankou here?

142
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:55,060
Ankou!

143
00:10:56,639 --> 00:10:58,320
Yes sir, right here!

144
00:10:58,935 --> 00:11:00,280
Please give your consent.

145
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,660
Make it really bright, now!

146
00:11:05,332 --> 00:11:06,993
That's a huge shell!

147
00:11:08,019 --> 00:11:11,440
Princess Otohime has shut herself inside that shell and won't come out.

148
00:11:11,655 --> 00:11:13,280
It's been a whole thousand years.

149
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:14,740
For a thousand years?

150
00:11:14,938 --> 00:11:17,093
Why did she lock herself in?

151
00:11:17,519 --> 00:11:20,446
Something terrible happened a thousand years ago.

152
00:11:20,899 --> 00:11:23,186
Sir Tink, you are our last hope.

153
00:11:23,445 --> 00:11:25,780
Please get my daughter out.

154
00:11:26,950 --> 00:11:29,219
Kai-san, Kai-san, open your lid!

155
00:11:35,129 --> 00:11:36,300
It's opening! It's opening!

156
00:11:38,099 --> 00:11:40,613
Kai-san, Kai-san, open it wider!

157
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:42,580
No, close the shell!

158
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:46,740
Otohime, w-wait... Otohime, don't close it!

159
00:11:46,765 --> 00:11:47,820
Don't close it!

160
00:11:48,259 --> 00:11:52,720
Kai-san, Kai-san, please open up. The Sea God wants to see Lady Otohime.

161
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:54,873
Hey, open your shell!

162
00:11:55,878 --> 00:11:56,960
What's wrong with the shell?

163
00:11:57,215 --> 00:11:58,720
Won't you listen to me?

164
00:11:58,830 --> 00:11:59,830
Close!

165
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,086
So, you're finally coming out.

166
00:12:06,110 --> 00:12:07,807
I've been waiting for you, Otohime.

167
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:15,960
Otohime, Otohime, why won't you come out?

168
00:12:16,669 --> 00:12:17,758
It's your fault.

169
00:12:17,782 --> 00:12:19,040
Why are you meddling?

170
00:12:19,325 --> 00:12:20,466
Get lost.

171
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:22,560
Shut up.

172
00:12:31,699 --> 00:12:32,993
Now, where did he go?

173
00:12:36,015 --> 00:12:39,386
Without Sapphire here, I'm hopeless.

174
00:12:41,469 --> 00:12:43,130
Tink!

175
00:12:43,502 --> 00:12:44,944
TINK!

176
00:12:44,968 --> 00:12:46,360
Where could Tink have gone?

177
00:12:47,063 --> 00:12:48,400
Feeling lonely, are we?

178
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:49,613
Shut up!

179
00:12:50,139 --> 00:12:53,320
My, my, I am Lord Sapphire's escort—that is to say, his bodyguard.

180
00:12:53,525 --> 00:12:55,999
You've got no right to tell me to shut up.

181
00:12:56,410 --> 00:12:57,586
I don't need a bodyguard.

182
00:12:57,650 --> 00:12:58,650
Stop following me.

183
00:13:00,761 --> 00:13:01,892
As long as I trail behind,

184
00:13:01,917 --> 00:13:03,625
I just might get the chance to

185
00:13:03,649 --> 00:13:06,213
strike you down and send you to the next world.

186
00:13:07,876 --> 00:13:11,100
Persistent and relentless—that's my best quality.

187
00:13:13,189 --> 00:13:14,926
They say a turtle came to pick Tink up.

188
00:13:15,589 --> 00:13:17,740
Yeah, he headed out toward the open sea.

189
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,013
Tink?

190
00:13:25,009 --> 00:13:27,393
Lord Sapphire, where are you going in that beat-up boat?

191
00:13:28,809 --> 00:13:29,993
I'm going to look for Tink!

192
00:13:31,969 --> 00:13:35,353
Tink! Tink!

193
00:13:37,013 --> 00:13:38,386
Talk about a stroke of luck!

194
00:13:39,139 --> 00:13:41,900
That junk boat will sink before it even gets offshore.

195
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:45,453
This is the end for Sapphire! Ah, what bliss!

196
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:48,220
Tink!

197
00:13:50,469 --> 00:13:52,166
Tink!

198
00:14:04,119 --> 00:14:07,113
Hey, hey! Let go of me!

199
00:14:07,250 --> 00:14:10,402
Sharks, you promised you wouldn't get rough.

200
00:14:10,426 --> 00:14:12,940
Yeah, well you're the one breaking your promise!

201
00:14:13,045 --> 00:14:16,000
I'll keep my promise! I definitely, definitely will!

202
00:14:16,534 --> 00:14:17,488
You mean it?

203
00:14:17,512 --> 00:14:18,882
 As promised a thousand years ago,

204
00:14:18,906 --> 00:14:21,088
you'll give me Otohime as my bride, right?

205
00:14:21,112 --> 00:14:21,646
 Yes.

206
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,600
His bride?!

207
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:25,980
Yes, absolutely.

208
00:14:27,202 --> 00:14:28,760
I really love Otohime.

209
00:14:28,875 --> 00:14:30,100
So, when will she show up?

210
00:14:31,005 --> 00:14:32,005
By the end of the day.

211
00:14:32,235 --> 00:14:34,415
It's useless. I can't wait any longer.

212
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:36,060
I've waited a thousand years for this!

213
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,660
I'll drag Otohime out my own way.

214
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,786
Yes, I'll definitely do it.

215
00:14:41,135 --> 00:14:41,920
Wait!

216
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,840
I'll be the one to summon Otohime.

217
00:14:44,125 --> 00:14:45,125
Wait.

218
00:14:45,365 --> 00:14:46,365
I can't wait any longer.

219
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,160
I'm doing this my way.

220
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,480
Got it?

221
00:14:52,039 --> 00:14:53,160
That nuisance is gone.

222
00:14:53,370 --> 00:14:55,266
Now, please bring her out this time.

223
00:14:55,529 --> 00:14:58,880
No, I don't want her marrying someone like Sharks!

224
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:00,060
That Tink.

225
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,773
Lady Otohime.

226
00:15:01,949 --> 00:15:06,626
You hid inside the shell because you didn't want to marry Sharks, right?

227
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:07,300
That's right.

228
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:08,736
But who are you?

229
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,320
I'm Tink.

230
00:15:10,695 --> 00:15:13,460
I'll protect you, so don't come out no matter what!

231
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:14,920
Sir Tink...

232
00:15:15,205 --> 00:15:18,160
A promise must always be kept.

233
00:15:18,539 --> 00:15:21,160
Why did you make such a foolish promise?

234
00:15:21,409 --> 00:15:23,108
To stop Shark's tyranny.

235
00:15:23,326 --> 00:15:25,882
He swore he'd stop picking on the weak fish

236
00:15:25,906 --> 00:15:28,000
if we gave him Otohime as his bride.

237
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:28,699
No way.

238
00:15:28,915 --> 00:15:31,000
I'll never let them open that shell!

239
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:32,000
Sir Tink...

240
00:15:32,150 --> 00:15:33,940
It's to protect the weak fish.

241
00:15:34,185 --> 00:15:35,338
Please try to understand.

242
00:15:35,470 --> 00:15:36,470
Hey, turtles!

243
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:38,560
Let's all protect Lady Otohime together!

244
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:40,515
That goes for the weak little fish, too, right?

245
00:15:40,539 --> 00:15:42,473
That's right. Let's all fight together!

246
00:15:43,439 --> 00:15:46,666
Tink doesn't know how terrifying the sharks are.

247
00:15:47,712 --> 00:15:49,780
A ship is passing above.

248
00:15:49,955 --> 00:15:50,955
That's right, sharks.

249
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:52,060
Drag the ship down!

250
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:54,246
And bring me some young maidens!

251
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:55,480
Yeah!

252
00:15:56,093 --> 00:15:58,339
Tink!

253
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,479
I just hope Tink is alive.

254
00:16:33,995 --> 00:16:36,060
I just hope she is alive... She's a perfect young maiden.

255
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:41,520
Now, the Pearl of Forgetfulness. Forget everything, and do as I command.

256
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:47,875
There we go. Now come along.

257
00:16:53,199 --> 00:16:55,593
Now then, let the fashion show begin!

258
00:16:59,105 --> 00:16:59,796
Young maiden,

259
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:02,640
put on the latest high-fashion dress and walk the runway.

260
00:17:12,232 --> 00:17:13,180
It's Sapphire!

261
00:17:13,414 --> 00:17:15,299
Wow, what a lovely outfit!

262
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:17,140
I'd love to show this to Otohime.

263
00:17:40,469 --> 00:17:43,600
Ah, this is magnificent! The absolute best!

264
00:17:45,802 --> 00:17:47,573
Buy 'em all!

265
00:18:01,879 --> 00:18:04,000
Sapphire, I'm so glad you came.

266
00:18:04,794 --> 00:18:07,093
Hey, Sapphire...

267
00:18:07,509 --> 00:18:09,420
Stop it! Who are you?

268
00:18:14,079 --> 00:18:15,079
Sapphire!

269
00:18:15,319 --> 00:18:18,060
Don't just stand there, save Lady Otohime!

270
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:19,426
Sapphire!

271
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,286
Sir Tink!

272
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:23,340
Where could he have gone?

273
00:18:23,489 --> 00:18:26,480
Great Sea God, let's gather the fish and fight Sharks!

274
00:18:27,699 --> 00:18:32,806
I'm afraid of fighting. Can't Sir Tink do something with his powers?

275
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Otohime!

276
00:18:42,710 --> 00:18:43,840
The wedding is about to start.

277
00:18:43,864 --> 00:18:44,446
Got it?

278
00:18:44,679 --> 00:18:47,520
You'll behave yourself once you're married, won't you, Sharks?

279
00:18:48,354 --> 00:18:49,460
Well, who knows?

280
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,560
Father!

281
00:18:51,584 --> 00:18:52,393
Otohime!

282
00:18:53,104 --> 00:18:53,946
Fool!

283
00:18:58,559 --> 00:19:00,200
What on earth happened?

284
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:02,720
- Giving up without a fight...
- I just don't get it.

285
00:19:03,314 --> 00:19:04,620
What are you talking about?

286
00:19:04,929 --> 00:19:07,720
No way! Who needs a Sapphire like this, anyway?

287
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:08,893
No, I hate you!

288
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,200
Tink!

289
00:19:12,469 --> 00:19:13,620
It's Tink!

290
00:19:16,019 --> 00:19:17,886
Why are we in a place like this?

291
00:19:18,419 --> 00:19:19,020
Why?

292
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:26,273
It opened!

293
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:26,933
Come on, Tink!

294
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:27,799
Hurry up!

295
00:19:32,989 --> 00:19:34,160
Hey, over here!

296
00:20:06,509 --> 00:20:09,800
Here comes Her Highness the bride!

297
00:20:13,859 --> 00:20:16,320
All right, let's begin.

298
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:22,494
Do you, Sharks, swear to take Otohime as your wife

299
00:20:22,518 --> 00:20:25,480
and live in peace without causing trouble?

300
00:20:26,970 --> 00:20:28,560
Well, I swear.

301
00:20:29,705 --> 00:20:33,494
Otohime, living with Sharks as your husband may seem impossible,

302
00:20:33,518 --> 00:20:39,660
but do you swear to endure it and live in peace?

303
00:20:41,483 --> 00:20:42,720
Are you embarrassed?

304
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,720
Do you swear?

305
00:20:45,073 --> 00:20:47,606
Answer already. I'm short-tempered.

306
00:20:48,084 --> 00:20:49,673
Swear to me, my Otohime.

307
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:50,815
Come on, swear it!

308
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:51,320
Or else!

309
00:20:52,446 --> 00:20:53,099
Hey, hold on!

310
00:21:08,299 --> 00:21:09,900
Put up a good fight!

311
00:21:12,900 --> 00:21:13,300
Take that!

312
00:21:13,674 --> 00:21:15,519
You're only tough when picking on the weak!

313
00:21:15,774 --> 00:21:16,780
Attack!

314
00:21:30,399 --> 00:21:31,500
Charge!

315
00:21:36,319 --> 00:21:37,680
Wow, way to go!

316
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:38,786
Oh, right!

317
00:21:42,660 --> 00:21:43,660
Kai-chan!

318
00:21:44,059 --> 00:21:45,940
Show your face!

319
00:21:46,261 --> 00:21:47,457
Hurry, hurry!

320
00:22:00,278 --> 00:22:02,399
Hey, I'm so glad I called you!

321
00:22:03,789 --> 00:22:04,620
Sir Tink!

322
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:05,800
That was great!

323
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:07,260
That was great!

324
00:22:15,854 --> 00:22:18,459
Thank you, Sapphire, Tink!

325
00:22:18,919 --> 00:22:20,146
I'm ashamed of myself!

326
00:22:20,219 --> 00:22:22,180
I completely forgot about fighting!

327
00:22:23,349 --> 00:22:24,620
What's wrong, Sapphire?

328
00:22:24,660 --> 00:22:25,660
This is terrible!

329
00:22:25,739 --> 00:22:27,130
In Urashima Taro, 

330
00:22:27,154 --> 00:22:32,017
one day in the Dragon Palace equals 50 years in the human world...

331
00:22:32,041 --> 00:22:32,519
Yikes!

332
00:22:32,769 --> 00:22:35,826
That means 50 years will have passed when we get back!

333
00:22:36,145 --> 00:22:37,038
Don't worry!

334
00:22:37,209 --> 00:22:39,260
Here, take this treasure box with you!

335
00:22:39,604 --> 00:22:40,720
I'm sure it will come in handy!

336
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:42,680
The treasure box...

337
00:22:43,760 --> 00:22:44,760
Goodbye!

338
00:22:45,014 --> 00:22:46,254
Goodbye!

339
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,633
Bye-Bye!

340
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:48,680
Goodbye!

341
00:22:53,529 --> 00:22:54,209
I'm so worried. 

342
00:22:54,233 --> 00:22:57,299
I wonder if all our friends have turned into old men by now...

343
00:23:09,134 --> 00:23:10,134
Nylon!

344
00:23:10,300 --> 00:23:11,300
What on earth happened?

345
00:23:11,564 --> 00:23:12,673
Everyone is frozen!

346
00:23:13,999 --> 00:23:14,896
What should we do?

347
00:23:16,973 --> 00:23:18,329
I-I'm kind of scared...

348
00:23:18,740 --> 00:23:19,339
Oh, I know!

349
00:23:19,429 --> 00:23:20,800
Let me open the treasure box!

350
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:26,460
If we open it, smoke might puff out and turn us into white-haired old folks!

351
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:37,226
We haven't changed! What a relief!

352
00:23:42,520 --> 00:23:43,620
Talk about a windfall!

353
00:23:43,854 --> 00:23:45,940
Sapphire drowned at sea!

354
00:23:46,350 --> 00:23:47,800
We'll make a fortune!

355
00:23:50,140 --> 00:23:50,773
Look at that!

356
00:23:51,069 --> 00:23:53,853
You two, I thought you were dead—what is going on here?

357
00:23:53,877 --> 00:23:55,877

